  "slug": "rna-binding-139a",
  "summary": "Recent simulations resolve how lipid, partner, and ligand binding propagate conformational changes to distal functional sites.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is simulation-based mapping of how local structural events couple to distal functional sites. In ezrin, MD simulations show PI(4,5)P2 binding to the FERM domain triggers spontaneous CTD dissociation, and T567 phosphorylation blocks reassociation. For CENP-A nucleosomes bound to CENP-N, SIRAH coarse-grained MD reports N-terminal flexibility, RG loop stabilization, and allosteric effects. Full-length P. aeruginosa ExsA simulations show the helix-turn-helix motif supports DNA binding while allosterically stabilizing the ligand-binding domain and exposing druggable pockets at the NTD/CTD interface. Enhanced-sampling TTMetaD simulations of SERINC3 propose a credit-card mechanism for phosphatidylserine scrambling. What is distinctive here is the attribution of specific allosteric routes and regulatory switches, such as phosphorylation gating of ezrin reassociation, to defined structural elements.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-13"
}
